The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
pm8350_die_temp {
    reg = <PM8350_ADC7_DIE_TEMP>;
    label = "pm8350_die_temp";
};
pmr735b_die_temp {
    reg = <PMR735B_ADC7_DIE_TEMP>;
    label = "pmr735b_die_temp";
};
```
Reason:
The inclusion of temperature sensor nodes for `pm8350` and `pmr735b` in the device tree configuration for the `sc7280-idp` board leads to incorrect device tree configurations since these PMICs are not present on the board, potentially causing system errors.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
-#include <dt-bindings/iio/qcom,spmi-adc7-pmr735b.h>
-#include <dt-bindings/iio/qcom,spmi-adc7-pm8350.h>
pmr735b_die_temp {
    reg = <PMR735B_ADC7_DIE_TEMP>;
    label = "pmr735b_die_temp";
};
```
Reason:
The removal of the `pm8350` and `pmr735b` temperature sensor nodes from the device tree configuration ensures that only the relevant PMICs are included, thus correcting the device tree for the `sc7280-idp` board and preventing potential system errors.

